    "title": "LESSON 12: THE PASSIVE WITH DI-",
    "header_color": "cyan",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 3,
        "content": [
          "   Jawaban itu ditulis di papan oleh",
          "   guru.",
          "   = The answer was written on the board",
          "     by the teacher.",
          "",
          "English keeps the passive for special",
          "occasions. Indonesian uses it constantly,",
          "and in places English never would.",
          "",
          "Swap meN- for di- and the sentence turns",
          "round. The thing done comes first, and",
          "the doer follows with oleh.",
          "",
          "   Guru menulis jawaban.              Press 1",
          "   = The teacher writes the answer.",
          "",
          "   Jawaban ditulis oleh guru.         Press 2",
          "   = The answer is written by the teacher."
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "Guru menulis jawaban.",
          "2": "Jawaban ditulis oleh guru."
        }
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 3,
        "content": [
          "Most of the time the doer is left out",
          "altogether, and oleh goes with it:",
          "",
          "   Buku itu dibaca di kelas.",
          "   = The book is read in class.",
          "",
          "That is the ordinary way to say what was",
          "done when who did it does not matter. On",
          "a sign it is the only way there is:",
          "",
          "   Dilarang masuk.",
          "   = No entry.",
          "The prefix di- is written closed up; the",
          "preposition di takes a space. Compare:",
          "",
          "   di jual  = at a place called Jual",
          "   dijual   = is being sold",
          "One space, two different sentences."
        ]
      },
      {
        "page": 3,
        "total_pages": 3,
        "content": [
          "When the doer is saya, kamu or kita, drop",
          "di- and put the pronoun straight before",
          "the bare root:",
          "",
          "   Buku itu saya baca.",
          "   = I read that book.",
          "   Surat itu sudah kamu tulis?",
          "   = Have you written that letter?",
          "",
          "Never 'dibaca oleh saya'. aku and kamu",
          "may shrink and glue on: kubaca, kaubaca.",
          "",
          "With dia, mereka or a name, di- comes",
          "back:",
          "   Buku itu dibaca oleh Budi.",
          "   = Budi read that book."
        ]
      }
