    "title": "LESSON 13: DOUBLED WORDS",
    "header_color": "cyan",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "   Setiap sore anak-anak mandi di sungai.",
          "   = Every afternoon the children bathe",
          "     in the river.",
          "",
          "Say the noun twice and you have a plural.",
          "The hyphen is compulsory: never anak anak",
          "and never anak2.",
          "",
          "   anak   a child   anak-anak   children",
          "   orang  a person  orang-orang people",
          "   buku   a book    buku-buku   books",
          "",
          "Indonesian does not need this often. A",
          "bare noun is already both: dua anak is",
          "two children. Double it when you mean",
          "many and no number is given.",
          "",
          "jalan-jalan means to go for a stroll."
        ]
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "Some doubled words are not plurals at",
          "all. They are single words that happen to",
          "be built twice, and their meaning is not",
          "the meaning of the half.",
          "",
          "   sama-sama      you're welcome",
          "   hati-hati      careful (not livers)",
          "   tiba-tiba      suddenly",
          "   laki-laki      a man",
          "   abu-abu        gray",
          "   masing-masing  each one",
          "   apa-apa        anything, nothing",
          "",
          "The cards mark these NOT A PLURAL in the",
          "notes. When you see that line, take the",
          "word whole and do not go looking for a",
          "root inside it."
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
