      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "   Dua ekor kucing sedang tidur.      Press 1",
          "   = Two cats are asleep.",
          "",
          "ekor means tail. Here it counts. Between",
          "a number and a noun Indonesian likes a",
          "counting word, the habit English keeps in",
          "two sheets of paper.",
          "",
          "   number + counter + noun",
          "",
          "   dua ekor kucing  = two cats",
          "   dua buah roti    = two loaves",
          "   dua orang guru   = two teachers",
          "",
          "Three counters carry almost everything:",
          "   orang for people",
          "   ekor for animals",
          "   buah for everything else"
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "Dua ekor kucing sedang tidur."
        }
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "se- in front of a counter means one, and",
          "the two run together as a single word:",
          "",
          "   seorang guru   one teacher",
          "   sebuah rumah   one house",
          "   seekor kucing  one cat",
          "",
          "Other nouns are borrowed as counters when",
          "the shape suits: lembar for sheets,",
          "batang for anything rod-shaped, potong",
          "for a cut piece, biji for small round",
          "things.",
          "",
          "   dua lembar kertas = two sheets of paper",
          "You are never obliged to use one. Dua",
          "kucing is understood everywhere, and in",
          "speech the counter is often dropped. In",
          "doubt, buah will not be wrong."
        ]
      }
