    "lesson_id": "015",
    "trigger_word": "mengatakan",
    "trigger_card_number": 151,
    "title": "LESSON 15: -KAN AND -I",
    "header_color": "cyan",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "   Dokter itu mengatakan bahwa saya harus",
          "   istirahat di rumah.",
          "   = The doctor said I must rest at home.",
          "",
          "mengatakan is meN- + kata + -kan. The",
          "prefix makes it a working verb; the",
          "ending gives it something to work on.",
          "",
          "   kata         a word",
          "   mengatakan   to say something",
          "",
          "   tunjuk       point",
          "   menunjukkan  to show something",
          "",
          "   putus        broken off",
          "   memutuskan   to decide something",
          "",
          "The root sits between the two."
        ]
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "-kan usually means do it TO something, or",
          "do it FOR someone.",
          "",
          "   Guru memberikan tugas kepada kami.",
          "   = The teacher gave us the work.",
          "",
          "-i is the other ending. It points at a",
          "place or a surface rather than a thing",
          "handed over.",
          "",
          "   Anak-anak harus dilindungi dari bahaya.",
          "   = Children must be protected from",
          "     danger.",
          "The pair is worth watching: one root will",
          "take both, with different senses.",
          "",
          "   menghubungkan = to join two things",
          "   menghubungi   = to get in touch with"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
